{ "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "MMC-VCI-V2.5-I01", "AIMName": "1MMC-VCI-V2.5-I01"},
  "Header":               "MMC-VCI-V2.5",

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Execution":            "Continuous",
  "OnDegraded":           "Continue",
  "Description":          "Voice Command Interface for Audio Scene Management (CAE-ASM): a person talks to the audio scene editor and it answers aloud. Automatic Speech Recognition recognises the speech; the JSON Interface of Audio Scene Management (1MMC-JSI-V2.5-I02, whose Access holds the schema of the User Command and the guide of the application) turns the request into a User Command in an Application JSON Instance, with the scene it is told of (ApplicationContext), and the User Command response into facts; Entity Dialogue Processing says what the facts say; Text to Speech speaks it. A command that is sent is not said: the person hears the application's answer when it arrives; a request that gives no command is answered at once, with what is missing.",

  "InternalTypes":        [],

